`plone-client profile set NAME KEY=VALUE…` changes some settings of an existing profile and leaves the others and its secret as they are, so one setting no longer needs `profile add --replace`, which asks for the secret again. `profile unset NAME KEY…` returns a setting to the defaults' value. The new profile is checked like any other before the configuration file is written, so an unknown key, a value of the wrong kind or an invalid value is refused and the file stays as it was; the name, `auth` and `secret` cannot be changed this way. @ericof
